{
  "name": "Scrolling Board",
  "description": "A tall board slides down toward a pressure line just above the conveyor. Clear boxes to let the stack compact upward and buy yourself room; anything that grinds into the line crumbles and floods the belt with noise. Survive to the end of the board.",
  "howToPlay": "Tap a box to release it together with its same-coloured neighbours. Every tap pushes the board one step down, so a tap that clears a lot is worth more than a tap that clears one. Cleared cells let the boxes below rise into them, which builds new same-coloured neighbours — that is your free chain. The pill in the top-left swaps between the tap-driven and auto-scrolling variants mid-run. If the conveyor fills up, you lose.",
  "author": "Prototype",
